  "description": "YAML and JSON intent files for C# and .NET: keep LLM instructions, result shapes, validation rules and examples outside compiled code. Run intents by name and check every reply in your process, with failed checks fed back within the configured limits. Supports primitive results, registered .NET types and JSON Schema shapes, plus an in-memory catalog. Intent files are versioned documents with revert. Supported saved edits reload while the application runs; malformed edits retain the last good definitions. New compiled result types, incompatible shapes, new named code checks and new call sites still need an application release. Reload is tested on local folders. Add this package to IntentSharp for file-backed or code-defined named intents; IntentSharp.Extensions.AI includes it. Commercial software, not open source: evaluate free for 30 days on development and test systems; after that, business use needs a paid license, and production use needs one from the first day (intentsharp.com/pricing).",
